hadiths[1]{hadithnumber,text}:
"1556","On the authority of Yusuf bin Musa, on the authority of Jarir, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Talha, on the authority of Abd al-Rahman Awsaja al-Nahmi, on the authority of al-Baraa ibn Azib, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, used to move the row from one side to another, and he would rub our shoulders or chests and say: “Do not disagree lest you disagree.” Your hearts.” He said: And he said: And he used to say: “Indeed, God and His angels send blessings upon those who pray in the first rows.” And I counted it, and I counted it. He said: “Adorn The Qur’an with your voices”"
